course: dictionary
lesson: 5586
title: Liar: a person who tells lies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A liar is a person who tells lies on purpose, saying things they know are not true to trick someone. The key word is know: a mistake is not lying, but a lie is said deliberately. «So there are two traps: believing every boast, or calling the boaster a liar and starting a fight.» The sentence shows that a liar can fool you, but calling someone a liar can also cause trouble.
explain: Calling someone a liar is a strong, rude thing to say, so think before you use it. If you think someone is not telling the truth, you can say, «I don't think that's true.» That is kinder, and it still tells the other person what you think. Be careful too: you cannot be sure someone is lying just because you disagree with them.
fact: A liar is a person who tells lies on purpose to trick someone.
fact: Calling someone a liar means you think they are not telling the truth.
fact: «A terrible liar» means someone who is bad at lying, so people can easily tell when they are not telling the truth.
fact: Calling someone a liar is a strong, rude thing to say, so «I don't think that's true» is often kinder.
fact: «Liar, liar, pants on fire» is a playground rhyme, not a rule about real life.
exercise: «So there are two traps: believing every boast, or calling the boaster a liar and starting a fight.» What is a liar? | *A person who tells lies on purpose to trick someone | A person who always tells the truth | A person who is very tall | A person who sings loudly
exercise: Mia thinks her friend is not telling the truth. Which kinder sentence could she use instead of «You're a liar!»? | Liar, liar, pants on fire | You are a big liar and a terrible liar | *I don't think that's true | Stop talking now
exercise: What does «a terrible liar» mean? | *Someone who is bad at lying | Someone who never tells any lies | Someone who forgets their words | Someone who is very kind to animals
test: A child says «I saw a dragon in the park» but knows it is not true, just to fool her friends. What is she? | *A liar | A winner | A reader | A helper
test: Why is calling someone a liar a strong thing to say? | It means they are very tall | It is always polite | *It is rude and can start a fight, so think carefully | It makes everyone laugh
exam: Ben knew the cake was gone and still said he had not touched it. What does liar mean? | *A person who says things they know are not true to trick someone | A person who bakes cakes | A person who is very hungry | A person who always tells the truth
